        <li>Volunteer at a dig, a museum store or a local heritage group, and watch real recording.</li>
        <li>Learn QGIS and basic mapping. The software is free.</li>
        <li>Practise photogrammetry on a small object or building with open-source software and a phone or camera.</li>
        <li>Read published excavation reports and copy how they structure a trench record.</li>
        <li>Use free lecture videos and open university material, and judge each course by whether it ends in a site record, a model or a report you can show.</li>
